                <pb facs="0844" n="716" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg716"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 536.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Foster</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6,
                        1885</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 349.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 343 of May 28
                    last, I now inclose a copy of a further dispatch from Havana in the case of the
                    fine on the American barkentine, Charles L. Pearson.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAS. D. PORTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>






